==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Extraterrestrial Envanz''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Extradimensional Envanz''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Despite being advertised as an [[Omni Strike]] unit, Mighty Carrowsell's first hit is [[Long Distance]], and because of that it will walk up to the base and stand at 1 range if there are no enemies preventing it from doing so.

Mighty Carrowsell is a crowd controller with Multi-Hit, [[Zombie Killer]] and 50% [[Slow]] and 100% [[Curse]] against Dark and Zombie enemies. They have very good survivability, boasting 74,800 health and 3 chances to reposition. Unfortunately, their survivability is nearly all they have going for them. For starters, their damage per second is very subpar, with only 4.4k DPS. Their DPS is only somewhat viable against Colossal enemies, giving them 6.6k DPS, but even then it's still not good. You're likely to get even less DPS than that, though, given their multi-hits have barely any pierce and can miss a lot especially since Dark and Zombie enemies tend to evade multi-hits with ease (via numerous repositions of Darks and burrowing of Zombies). As such their generalist capabilities are out of the question.

While their Curse only needs one of the multi-hits to connect per attack to be permanent, it is of little utility because it only kills abilities, not the stat-based threats in its targeted traits. [[Big Peng Z]] (who relies on Zombie/Dark peons for pressure), [[Le'Grim]], and very occasionally [[Lord Gravey]] are the only noteworthy enemies, since the unit is already Immune to Toxic and will likely kill Zollow outright. Lastly, their slow can never reach full uptime. And, as previously mentioned, Dark and zombies will likely just evade lots of Mighty Carrowsell's attacks, so their slow is very pitiful. Housewife and Bomber Cat are much better options for controlling Zombies and Darks respectively for the most part.

==='''True Form'''===
Extradimensional Envanz gains the Resistance ability against their target traits. This helps to drastically improve their survivability, going from 74,800 Base Health to a massive 374,000 HP against both Dark and Zombie enemies, and if including [[Colossus Slayer]] added to that, their total is a gargantuan 486,200 Health against Big Peng Z and Le'Grim! They can finally withstand hits from their target traits, and become a reliable, tanky Crowd-Controller, although their utility remains questionable beyond Big Peng Z.

Also, with the damage bonus, they now do 51,000 damage total, which goes up to 81,600 damage against Colossal Enemies. This damage increase is helpful, but not great. But keep in mind that many other Ubers can exceed the list of enemies that may be countered.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Move Speed Up''' is of utmost importance. Envanz's most annoying quirk is its sluggish pace that prevents it from ever reaching the frontlines in a timely manner. This Talent triples their speed from 5 to 15, now keeping up with the rest of your attackers. You can even stop halfway if 15 speed sounds like too much for your liking, or if investing in Envanz's Talents is too much of a madman's endeavor.

'''Slow''' is straightforward, but not very worth it due to the meager 1-second increase it so graciously grants on an ability that doesn't even activate 100% of the time.

While '''[[Soulstrike]]''' appears favorable for Envanz, the blind spot within the Omni Strike's effective range means Envanz cannot hit Zombies wedged directly inside of it. What this means is that it will occasionally get stuck in a cycle of attacking literally nothing if a Zombie dies in the wrong place. It can still be useful, allowing Envanz a platform to utilize its pierce, but the Talent is overall very questionable.

Don't bother with '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Freeze]]''', it does nothing in most situations. Its best case scenarios are against [[Deathshund]] and [[Death Angel Z-Onel]], neither of which warrant this Talent to counter.

Finally, '''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' are what you would expect, but be sure to upgrade Envanz with [[Catseye]]s before even think about upgrading them. You shouldn't be considering it at all though, it's unhealthy.

